course: dictionary
lesson: 6766
title: One word, many jobs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the words around them show which meaning the writer wants. The word operator can mean a person who works a machine, a person who answers phone calls, a company that runs a service, or a maths symbol. In «When you call 999, you answer the operator's questions», the operator is a person who asks you questions.
explain: Context is the words and sentences around a word, and they leave clues. In «The crane operator lifted the steel beams», the clue is crane, so an operator is a person who works a machine. Check your meaning by swapping it in: a crane operator is someone who runs a crane, and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: In maths, an operator is a sign like + − × ÷. The clues are numbers and sums, not people. In «Which operator should you use here, + or ×?», the operator is a sign. Same word, different meaning. Always ask: what are the words around it about?
fact: Operator is a noun, and its plural is operators.
fact: An operator can be a person who works a machine, like «a crane operator».
fact: An operator can be a person who answers calls, like an emergency operator.
fact: «Operator» can also mean a company that runs a service, like «a tour operator» or «a mobile phone operator».
fact: In maths, + − × and ÷ are operators, because they tell you which operation to do.
exercise: «When you call 999, you answer the operator's questions.» Who is the operator here? | A bus driver on a tour | A maths symbol like + | *A person who answers the call and sends help | A machine inside the phone
exercise: In the sum 6 × 4 = 24, which symbol is the operator? | 4 | 6 | *× | =
exercise: Nadia reads «a tour operator». What does tour operator probably mean? | A machine that cuts grass | A sign used in sums | *A company that runs trips for holidaymakers | A person who only drives a tour bus
test: «Connect me to an operator, please», the caller says. What does operator mean here? | *A person who answers calls and connects people | A crane worker on a building site | A company that makes phones | A plus sign used in maths
test: Jayden says operator can only mean a maths sign. Is he right? | Yes, always, in every sentence | *No, it can also mean a person or a company | No, it only means a machine | Yes, but only in science lessons
exam: Which meaning fits «The operator asked where I was and which service I needed»? | A symbol for multiplying | A machine that prints tickets | A company that sells phone credit | *A person who answers emergency calls
